1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,400
It's two in the morning. And that charge wasn't you.

2
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:16,400
In Latin America, fraud costs financial firms over three and a half times what was stolen.

3
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,500
Poor automation, and you block the wrong card.

4
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,600
Wait, and the card stays open.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,900
The hard part isn't answering. It's deciding safely.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,600
Introducing Pattern Blue. Customer service for banks that knows when to act, when to ask, and when to hand off.

7
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:48,600
It acts. The card is blocked in the conversation, and it only says so after the bank's own database confirms it.

8
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,800
Every action, a receipt.

9
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:08,000
It asks. A small model inside the bank, grounded in how Latin America really writes, reads every message in about twenty milliseconds.

10
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:11,800
When it isn't sure, it asks first.

11
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:21,600
And it knows when to stop. A dispute goes to a person, with a brief, not a transcript.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:38,400
Here's the difference. The language model writes the words and proposes the action. But it holds no keys.

13
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:51,200
Three deterministic checks decide: the state of the conversation, the bank's policy, and the database.

14
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:57,600
Even when someone tries to talk it out of the rules.

15
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,000
The AI has a voice. Not a vote.

16
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:09,400
Zero unsafe actions across fifty-eight live scenarios.

17
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,800
About a twentieth of a cent per conversation.

18
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:18,600
And because safety lives in the core: swap the model, keep the safety.

19
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,400
One more thing.

20
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:28,400
Your risk team can change a policy, or switch on a whole new workflow, in seconds.

21
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:32,800
No code. No deploy. Every change on a hash-chained ledger.

22
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,600
Next episode: Pattern Blue, in your bank.

23
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:51,200
Pattern Blue. The AI has a voice. Not a vote.
